# inventory, equipment, compare, examine and read, with Hoarder in the temple. Hoarder wears a large metal shield,
# wields a long sword and wears an invisible leather cap (so equipment says "something."); carries two daggers, a
# small sword, two shields, a bag with a cup of water in it, a bottle of beer and a water skin.
@connect hoard
Hoarder
psswrd
@return
inventory
combine
inventory
combine
equipment
# compare: nothing, what Hoarder hasn't got, what Hoarder wears (get_obj_carry skips it), each to what's worn, to
# itself, to an object of another type, two drink containers (a type compare doesn't rank), and better, worse and the
# same.
compare
compare zz
compare cap
compare dagger
compare wooden
compare bag
compare dagger zz
compare dagger dagger
compare dagger 2.dagger
compare dagger bag
compare bottle skin
compare sword dagger
compare wooden small
compare metal wooden
compare 2.small wooden
# examine: nothing, what isn't here, and each kind it says more about. Coin piles (3132) with values set: no coins,
# one gold, gold, one silver, silver, and both.
examine
examine zz
examine dagger
examine bag
examine bottle
examine skin
@obj 3132 3001 0 0 0 0 0
examine coins
@obj 3132 3001 0 1 0 0 0
examine coins
@obj 3132 3001 0 7 0 0 0
examine coins
@obj 3132 3001 1 0 0 0 0
examine coins
@obj 3132 3001 9 0 0 0 0
examine coins
@obj 3132 3001 4 3 0 0 0
examine coins
# The container branch looks "in" the whole argument, not just its first word.
examine bag foo
@obj 3010 3001 10000 0 0 1000 100
examine pit
read dagger
read
